        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cc64ae97-f1e0-5645-a4ae-403e7af49b72",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin DuBrow, Lance King\n- Organizations: Quiet Riot, Nightmare Records\n- Products: QR III, Terrified\n- Roles: heavy metal singer, lead vocalist, record label founder\n\nFacts:\n- Kevin DuBrow was an American heavy metal singer born on October 29, 1955, and he died on November 19, 2007.\n- Kevin DuBrow was the lead vocalist of Quiet Riot from 1975 to 1987 and again from 1990 until his death in 2007.\n- Lance King was born on November 23, 1962, and he is an American heavy metal vocalist specializing in melodic rock, progressive metal, and power metal.\n- Lance King started the record label Nightmare in 1990 to release his own music, and he has remained in charge of the label.\n- QR III was the last album to feature lead singer Kevin DuBrow until the 1993 album Terrified.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
